      "id": "xmet:0000300",
      "type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "quinone formation",
      "inScheme": "xmet:scheme",
      "definition": "Formation of a quinone species by metabolic oxidation (quinone, quinone-imine, quinone-methide, or imine-methide). Pathway depth is the dependency cone into terminating dehydrogenation (precedes-ancestors ∪ DH), not raw elementary-plan length — free unrelated steps do not deepen the count. From the quinone-formation and Metabolic Forest papers; under dehydrogenation in the Forest-mapped Phase I hierarchy.",
      "altLabel": [
        "quinonation",
        "quinone species formation"
      ],
      "broader": "xmet:0000001",
